course: dictionary
lesson: 11974
title: When power changes hands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cede means to give something up to someone else, such as land, power or rights. Read the context to work it out: «After the war, the country had to cede land to its neighbour.» The clues are after the war and had to. The country lost something and had to hand it over.
explain: Cede is a formal word, so you will meet it in history, news and politics. It tells you that control is moving from one person or country to another. Ask yourself: who has to give something up, and who gets it? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word and check it still makes sense.
explain: Cede can also be used in sport. «The team ceded possession of the ball in the final minute.» The team gave the ball away to the other side. The word is the same, but the thing being given up is different.
fact: Cede means to give up land, power or rights to someone else.
fact: Cede is a formal word, often found in history books, politics and the news.
fact: In 1842 China ceded Hong Kong to Britain, which means China handed control of it over to Britain.
fact: Spain ceded Florida, which means Spain gave up control of Florida.
fact: In sport, to cede possession means to give the ball or the advantage away to the other team.
exercise: «After the war, the country had to cede land to its neighbour.» What does cede mean? | *Give up to someone else | Keep safely | Build a wall around | Sell in a shop
exercise: In 1842 China ceded Hong Kong to Britain. What did China do? | Built a new city | Asked Britain for a holiday | Won a football match | *Handed control of Hong Kong over to Britain
exercise: «The team ceded possession of the ball in the final minute.» What did the team do with the ball? | Painted it blue | *Gave it away to the other team | Kept it hidden in the goal | Kicked it into the sky
test: «The old king would not cede his power, even when the people asked.» What did the king refuse to do? | Sing a song to the people | *Give up his power | Build a bridge over the river
test: Which word means the same as cede? | Hold on to | *Hand over | Guard | Keep
exam: The company agreed to ___ control of the shop to its rival. | Paint | Count | *Cede | Keep
